  /* ── packages/skill-memo-ilife/src/sync/feishu.ts（#1225 迁入） ── */
  'skill-memo-ilife.sync-feishu.c001': "The Feishu CLI website is: https://www.feishu.cn/feishu-cli",
  'skill-memo-ilife.sync-feishu.c002': "Install and configure the Feishu CLI (lark-cli) on this machine. You drive it; keep going until it is done.\n\nEnd state that must hold (actually run each command and paste back the command and its output):\n1) lark-cli --version >= 1.0.82 (older versions lack the --no-wait we need)\n2) where lark-cli (Windows) or which lark-cli (macOS/Linux) resolves; on Windows also confirm the file %APPDATA%\\npm\\lark-cli.cmd exists\n3) lark-cli auth status output contains identities.user.openId\n4) lark-cli auth check --scope task exits 0 (paste the exit code too) — Memo needs the task scope\n5) lark-cli calendar +agenda exits 0 (paste the exit code too) — Schedule needs to read your primary calendar\n6) The skill side works too: run Schedule's \"Feishu probe\" once (a sync probe that writes nothing) and it must not report \"CLI missing / not logged in / calendar unreachable\"\n\nHow to do it:\n7) If Node.js/npm is unavailable, install it first.\n8) Install: npm install -g @larksuite/cli. Install only this official package (its bin is lark-cli); do not install the lark-cli package from npm.\n9) Also do the second item in the official guide: npx -y skills add https://open.feishu.cn --skill -y\n10) Configure and log in exactly as these two say (both are the CLI's own --help wording written for AI agents; do not rewrite them):\n    Initialize first: lark-cli config init --new\n      It blocks waiting for you to finish browser authorization, so start it in the background and pull the verification URL out of its output\n      (CLI wording: Run it in the background and retrieve the verification URL from its output);\n      give me the link, and continue once I approve.\n      If it is rejected with something like Inside an Agent context, follow its hint and switch to lark-cli config bind.\n    Then authorize: lark-cli auth login --no-wait --json --domain calendar,task\n      It returns a verification link (or QR code) immediately; give me the link, and after I approve finish with\n      lark-cli auth login --device-code <the device code you got>.\n    Official guide: https://open.feishu.cn/document/no_class/mcp-archive/feishu-cli-installation-guide.md\n    Subcommands follow lark-cli auth --help / config --help and the official docs; do not guess. When done, items 3, 4, 5 must pass.\n11) If the npm global directory is not on the system PATH, add it to the system PATH (not just export it in the current terminal).\n\nHow to proceed:\n12) Except for the three cases in item 13, finish everything yourself in one go without asking me step by step: install, edit PATH, retry, fix errors.\n13) Only these three need me; when one comes up, use /wizard to generate a script that walks me through it, and when it is done keep going automatically:\n    ① browser-based initialization authorization / login (give me the verification link or QR code);\n    ② system permission prompts (administrator/sudo);\n    ③ Node.js, where I must first decide how to install it.\n14) If any step fails: fix it yourself from the error; if you cannot, tell me once \"where it is stuck, the exact error, and what I need to do\".\n\nReference site: https://www.feishu.cn/feishu-cli",
